WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.212
After identifying a quality problem we still need a
response Sometimes

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:12.149
we can correct a value Sometimes we retain it
Sometimes we exclude

00:00:12.176 --> 00:00:17.755
it from one analysis without deleting it from the
source Sometimes we impute missing

00:00:17.781 --> 00:00:23.297
information Often a quality flag is the most
transparent choice

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:28.824
when uncertainty remains The objective is not to
make the dataset look

00:00:28.851 --> 00:00:33.419
perfect It is to make limitations explicit and
manageable
